IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc14-part12-currency.l4 -- PART XII "Offences Relating to Currency" (ss 448 to 462) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`) for Punishment, Imprisonment, Fine, Class of offence and the length-of-time constants.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc14)"):
--   JUST TRUE   the facts bring the case within the provision, on the text's own words;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" or "unless" or "where" that fails, a flat negative such as "does not apply");
--   NOTHING     not covered: the provision lists without closing the list, says "includes", or limits a prohibition in its own wording ("without lawful justification or excuse",
--               "knowingly", the conduct it names) and the case falls outside the limit. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- An offence section is answered by three functions: whether the facts bring the person within it (MAYBE BOOLEAN), the class of offence it makes, and its punishment, one Punishment per limb.
-- Where a fact is a term defined in section 448 (counterfeit money, a counterfeit token of value, current), the answer of that definition is taken as an input named for it.

§ `PART XII -- Offences Relating to Currency`

§§ `s 448 -- Definitions ("In this Part,")`

-- src:7879 | 448 In this Part,
-- src:7880 | counterfeit money includes
-- src:7881 | (a) a false coin or false paper money that resembles or is apparently intended to resemble or pass for a current coin or current paper money,
-- src:7882 | (b) a forged bank-note or forged blank bank-note, whether complete or incomplete,
-- src:7883 | (c) a genuine coin or genuine paper money that is prepared or altered to resemble or pass for a current coin or current paper money of a higher denomination,
-- src:7884 | (d) a current coin from which the milling is removed by filing or cutting the edges and on which new milling is made to restore its appearance,
-- src:7885 | (e) a coin cased with gold, silver or nickel, as the case may be, that is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin, and
-- src:7886 | (f) a coin or a piece of metal or mixed metals that is washed or coloured by any means with a wash or material capable of producing the appearance of gold, silver or nickel and that is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin; (monnaie contrefaite)
@ref s 448 "counterfeit money" (src:7879-7886)
GIVEN `a false coin or false paper money that resembles or is apparently intended to resemble or pass for a current coin or current paper money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a forged bank-note or forged blank bank-note, whether complete or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a genuine coin or genuine paper money that is prepared or altered to resemble or pass for a current coin or current paper money of a higher denomination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a current coin from which the milling is removed by filing or cutting the edges and on which new milling is made to restore its appearance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a coin cased with gold, silver or nickel, as the case may be, that is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a coin or a piece of metal or mixed metals that is washed or coloured by any means with a wash or material capable of producing the appearance of gold, silver or nickel and that is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448 counterfeit money` MEANS
    IF `a false coin or false paper money that resembles or is apparently intended to resemble or pass for a current coin or current paper money`   -- (a)
        OR `a forged bank-note or forged blank bank-note, whether complete or incomplete`   -- (b)
        OR `a genuine coin or genuine paper money that is prepared or altered to resemble or pass for a current coin or current paper money of a higher denomination`   -- (c)
        OR `a current coin from which the milling is removed by filing or cutting the edges and on which new milling is made to restore its appearance`   -- (d)
        OR `a coin cased with gold, silver or nickel, as the case may be, that is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin`   -- (e)
        OR `a coin or a piece of metal or mixed metals that is washed or coloured by any means with a wash or material capable of producing the appearance of gold, silver or nickel and that is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin`   -- (f)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "counterfeit money includes"

-- src:7887 | counterfeit token of value means a counterfeit excise stamp, postage stamp or other evidence of value, by whatever technical, trivial or deceptive designation it may be described, and includes genuine coin or paper money that has no value as money; (symbole de valeur contrefait)
@ref s 448 "counterfeit token of value" (src:7887)
GIVEN `a counterfeit excise stamp, postage stamp or other evidence of value, by whatever technical, trivial or deceptive designation it may be described` IS A BOOLEAN
      `genuine coin or paper money that has no value as money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448 counterfeit token of value` MEANS
    IF `a counterfeit excise stamp, postage stamp or other evidence of value, by whatever technical, trivial or deceptive designation it may be described`
        OR `genuine coin or paper money that has no value as money`   -- "and includes genuine coin or paper money that has no value as money"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "counterfeit token of value means a counterfeit excise stamp, postage stamp or other evidence of value"

-- src:7888 | current means lawfully current in Canada or elsewhere by virtue of a law, proclamation or regulation in force in Canada or elsewhere as the case may be; (courant)
@ref s 448 "current" (src:7888)
GIVEN `lawfully current in Canada or elsewhere by virtue of a law, proclamation or regulation in force in Canada or elsewhere as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448 current` MEANS
    IF `lawfully current in Canada or elsewhere by virtue of a law, proclamation or regulation in force in Canada or elsewhere as the case may be`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "current means lawfully current in Canada or elsewhere"

-- src:7889 | utter includes sell, pay, tender and put off. (mettre en circulation)
@ref s 448 "utter" (src:7889)
DECLARE `s 448 act of uttering` IS ONE OF
    `s 448 sell`
    `s 448 pay`
    `s 448 tender`
    `s 448 put off`
    `s 448 an act that is none of those named`

@ref s 448 "utter" (src:7889)
GIVEN act IS A `s 448 act of uttering`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448 utter` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 448 sell` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 448 pay` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 448 tender` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 448 put off` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 448 an act that is none of those named` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "utter includes sell, pay, tender and put off"

§§ `Punishments used below (one Punishment per limb; the core's Punishment record)`

-- A limb that says "guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding N".
GIVEN term IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` term, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- A limb that says only "guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction": the section states no term and no fine
-- (the general summary-conviction penalty is in Part XXVII, another part).
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 454 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§§ `s 449 -- Making`

-- src:7893 | 449 Every one who makes or begins to make counterfeit money is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 449 (src:7893)
GIVEN `the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `makes or begins to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 449 the person commits the offence of making counterfeit money` MEANS
    IF `makes or begins to make it` AND `the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "makes or begins to make counterfeit money"

@ref s 449 (src:7893)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 449 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 449 (src:7893)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 449 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `fourteen years`

§§ `s 450 -- Possession, etc., of counterfeit money`

-- src:7897 | 450 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who, without lawful justification or excuse,
-- src:7898 | (a) buys, receives or offers to buy or receive counterfeit money;
-- src:7899 | (b) has in their custody or possession counterfeit money; or
-- src:7900 | (c) introduces counterfeit money into Canada.
@ref s 450 (src:7897-7900)
GIVEN `the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `without lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `buys, receives or offers to buy or receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has it in their custody or possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `introduces it into Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 450 the person commits the offence of possessing, etc., counterfeit money` MEANS
    IF `without lawful justification or excuse`
        AND (`buys, receives or offers to buy or receive it` OR `has it in their custody or possession` OR `introduces it into Canada`)   -- (a), (b), (c)
        AND `the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful justification or excuse"

@ref s 450 (src:7897-7900)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 450 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 450 (src:7897)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 450 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `fourteen years`

§§ `s 451 -- Having clippings, etc.`

-- src:7902 | 451 Every person who, without lawful justification or excuse, has in their custody or possession gold or silver filings, clippings or bullion or gold or silver in dust, solution or otherwise, produced or obtained by impairing, diminishing or lightening a current gold or silver coin, knowing that it has been so produced or obtained, is guilty of
-- src:7903 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7904 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 451 (src:7902-7904)
GIVEN `without lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has in their custody or possession gold or silver filings, clippings or bullion or gold or silver in dust, solution or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `produced or obtained by impairing, diminishing or lightening a current gold or silver coin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowing that it has been so produced or obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 451 the person commits the offence of having clippings, etc.` MEANS
    IF `without lawful justification or excuse`
        AND `has in their custody or possession gold or silver filings, clippings or bullion or gold or silver in dust, solution or otherwise`
        AND `produced or obtained by impairing, diminishing or lightening a current gold or silver coin`
        AND `knowing that it has been so produced or obtained`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful justification or excuse, has in their custody or possession gold or silver filings, clippings or bullion"

@ref s 451 (src:7902-7904)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 451 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 451 (src:7903-7904)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 451 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `five years`   -- (a)
       , `s 454 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`   -- (b)

§§ `s 452 -- Uttering, etc., counterfeit money`

-- src:7908 | 452 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who, without lawful justification or excuse,
-- src:7909 | (a) utters or offers to utter counterfeit money or uses counterfeit money as if it were genuine, or
-- src:7910 | (b) exports, sends or takes counterfeit money out of Canada.
@ref s 452 (src:7908-7910)
GIVEN `the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `without lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `utters or offers to utter it or uses it as if it were genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exports, sends or takes it out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 452 the person commits the offence of uttering, etc., counterfeit money` MEANS
    IF `without lawful justification or excuse`
        AND (`utters or offers to utter it or uses it as if it were genuine` OR `exports, sends or takes it out of Canada`)   -- (a), (b)
        AND `the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful justification or excuse"

@ref s 452 (src:7908)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 452 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 452 (src:7908)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 452 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `fourteen years`

§§ `s 453 -- Uttering coin`

-- src:7912 | 453 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, with intent to defraud, knowingly utters
-- src:7913 | (a) a coin that is not current, or
-- src:7914 | (b) a piece of metal or mixed metals that resembles in size, figure or colour a current coin for which it is uttered.
@ref s 453 (src:7912-7914)
GIVEN `with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowingly utters it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing uttered is a coin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coin is current, by s 448 current` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing uttered is a piece of metal or mixed metals that resembles in size, figure or colour a current coin for which it is uttered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 453 the person commits the offence of uttering coin` MEANS
    IF NOT (`with intent to defraud` AND `knowingly utters it`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with intent to defraud, knowingly utters"
    ELSE IF `the thing uttered is a piece of metal or mixed metals that resembles in size, figure or colour a current coin for which it is uttered`
         THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
         ELSE IF `the thing uttered is a coin`
              THEN CONSIDER `the coin is current, by s 448 current`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the coin is current is itself not covered
                   WHEN JUST c THEN IF c THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a coin that is not current" is not met when the coin is current
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a coin that is not current, or"

@ref s 453 (src:7912-7914)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 453 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 453 (src:7912)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 453 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `two years`
       , `s 454 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`

§§ `s 454 -- Slugs and tokens`

-- src:7916 | 454 Every person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, without lawful excuse, manufactures, produces, sells or has in their possession anything that is intended to be fraudulently used in substitution for a coin or token of value that any coin or token-operated device is designed to receive.
@ref s 454 (src:7916)
GIVEN `without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `manufactures, produces, sells or has in their possession anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is intended to be fraudulently used in substitution for a coin or token of value that any coin or token-operated device is designed to receive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 454 the person commits the offence concerning slugs and tokens` MEANS
    IF `without lawful excuse`
        AND `manufactures, produces, sells or has in their possession anything`
        AND `it is intended to be fraudulently used in substitution for a coin or token of value that any coin or token-operated device is designed to receive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse, manufactures, produces, sells or has in their possession anything"

@ref s 454 (src:7916)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 454 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 454 (src:7916)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 454 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 454 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`

§§ `s 455 -- Clipping and uttering clipped coin`

-- src:7920 | 455 Every one who
-- src:7921 | (a) impairs, diminishes or lightens a current gold or silver coin with intent that it should pass for a current gold or silver coin, or
-- src:7922 | (b) utters a coin knowing that it has been impaired, diminished or lightened contrary to paragraph (a),
-- src:7923 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 455 (src:7920-7923)
GIVEN `the coin is current, by s 448 current` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the coin is a gold or silver coin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `impairs, diminishes or lightens it with intent that it should pass for a current gold or silver coin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `utters a coin knowing that it has been impaired, diminished or lightened contrary to paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 455 the person commits the offence of clipping or of uttering clipped coin` MEANS
    IF (`the coin is a gold or silver coin` AND `the coin is current, by s 448 current` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `impairs, diminishes or lightens it with intent that it should pass for a current gold or silver coin`)   -- (a)
        OR `utters a coin knowing that it has been impaired, diminished or lightened contrary to paragraph (a)`   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "impairs, diminishes or lightens a current gold or silver coin with intent that it should pass"

@ref s 455 (src:7923)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 455 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 455 (src:7923)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 455 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `fourteen years`

§§ `s 456 -- Defacing current coins`

-- src:7925 | 456 Every one who
-- src:7926 | (a) defaces a current coin, or
-- src:7927 | (b) utters a current coin that has been defaced,
-- src:7928 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 456 (src:7925-7928)
GIVEN `the coin is current, by s 448 current` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `defaces it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `utters it after it has been defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 456 the person commits the offence of defacing current coins` MEANS
    IF (`defaces it` OR `utters it after it has been defaced`) AND `the coin is current, by s 448 current` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a), (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "defaces a current coin"

@ref s 456 (src:7928)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 456 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 456 (src:7928)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 456 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 454 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`

§§ `s 457 -- Likeness of bank-notes`

-- src:7930 | 457 (1) No person shall make, publish, print, execute, issue, distribute or circulate, including by electronic or computer-assisted means, anything in the likeness of
-- src:7931 | (a) a current bank-note; or
-- src:7932 | (b) an obligation or a security of a government or bank.
@ref s 457(1) (src:7930-7932)
GIVEN `makes, publishes, prints, executes, issues, distributes or circulates anything, including by electronic or computer-assisted means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the likeness of a bank-note, and the bank-note is current, by s 448 current` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is in the likeness of an obligation or a security of a government or bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 457(1) the conduct is prohibited` MEANS
    IF `makes, publishes, prints, executes, issues, distributes or circulates anything, including by electronic or computer-assisted means`
        AND (`it is in the likeness of a bank-note, and the bank-note is current, by s 448 current` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
             OR `it is in the likeness of an obligation or a security of a government or bank`)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person shall make, publish, print, execute, issue, distribute or circulate"

-- src:7934 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to
-- src:7935 | (a) the Bank of Canada or its employees when they are carrying out their duties;
-- src:7936 | (b) the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or its members or employees when they are carrying out their duties; or
-- src:7937 | (c) any person acting under a contract or licence from the Bank of Canada or Royal Canadian Mounted Police.
@ref s 457(2) (src:7934-7937)
GIVEN `the Bank of Canada or its employees when they are carrying out their duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or its members or employees when they are carrying out their duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any person acting under a contract or licence from the Bank of Canada or Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 457(2) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the Bank of Canada or its employees when they are carrying out their duties`   -- (a)
        OR `the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or its members or employees when they are carrying out their duties`   -- (b)
        OR `any person acting under a contract or licence from the Bank of Canada or Royal Canadian Mounted Police`   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Subsection (1) does not apply to"

-- src:7939 | (3) A person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 457(3) (src:7939)
GIVEN `contravenes subsection (1), by s 457(1) the conduct is prohibited` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 457(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 457(3) the person commits the offence of contravening subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 457(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to"
    ELSE IF `contravenes subsection (1), by s 457(1) the conduct is prohibited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who contravenes subsection (1)"

@ref s 457(3) (src:7939)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 457(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 457(3) (src:7939)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 457(3) the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 454 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`

-- src:7941 | (4) No person shall be convicted of an offence under subsection (3) in relation to the printed likeness of a Canadian bank-note if it is established that the length or width of the likeness is less than three-fourths or greater than one-and-one-half times the length or width, as the case may be, of the bank-note and
-- src:7942 | (a) the likeness is in black-and-white only; or
-- src:7943 | (b) the likeness of the bank-note appears on only one side of the likeness.
@ref s 457(4) (src:7941-7943)
GIVEN `the offence is under subsection (3) in relation to the printed likeness of a Canadian bank-note` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the length of the likeness, as a multiple of the length of the bank-note` IS A NUMBER
      `the width of the likeness, as a multiple of the width of the bank-note` IS A NUMBER
      `the likeness is in black-and-white only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the likeness of the bank-note appears on only one side of the likeness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 457(4) the defence of a likeness of a different size applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence is under subsection (3) in relation to the printed likeness of a Canadian bank-note`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the printed likeness of a Canadian bank-note"
    ELSE IF (`the length of the likeness, as a multiple of the length of the bank-note` LESS THAN 0.75
                OR `the length of the likeness, as a multiple of the length of the bank-note` GREATER THAN 1.5
                OR `the width of the likeness, as a multiple of the width of the bank-note` LESS THAN 0.75
                OR `the width of the likeness, as a multiple of the width of the bank-note` GREATER THAN 1.5)   -- "the length or width, as the case may be": either dimension (fork)
            AND (`the likeness is in black-and-white only` OR `the likeness of the bank-note appears on only one side of the likeness`)   -- (a), (b)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is established that the length or width of the likeness is less than three-fourths or greater than one-and-one-half times" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

§§ `s 458 -- Making, having or dealing in instruments for counterfeiting`

-- src:7947 | 458 Every person who, without lawful justification or excuse, makes, repairs, buys, sells or has in their custody or possession any machine, engine, tool, instrument, material or other thing that they know has been used or is adapted and intended for use in making counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref s 458 (src:7947)
GIVEN `without lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `makes, repairs, buys, sells or has in their custody or possession any machine, engine, tool, instrument, material or other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they know it has been used or is adapted and intended for use in making counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 458 the person commits the offence concerning instruments for counterfeiting` MEANS
    IF `without lawful justification or excuse`
        AND `makes, repairs, buys, sells or has in their custody or possession any machine, engine, tool, instrument, material or other thing`
        AND `they know it has been used or is adapted and intended for use in making counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful justification or excuse, makes, repairs, buys, sells or has in their custody or possession"

@ref s 458 (src:7947)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 458 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 458 (src:7947)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 458 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `fourteen years`

§§ `s 459 -- Conveying instruments for coining out of mint`

-- src:7949 | 459 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who, without lawful justification or excuse, knowingly conveys out of any of Her Majesty’s mints in Canada,
-- src:7950 | (a) any machine, engine, tool, instrument, material or thing used or employed in connection with the manufacture of coins,
-- src:7951 | (b) a useful part of anything mentioned in paragraph (a), or
-- src:7952 | (c) coin, bullion, metal or a mixture of metals.
@ref s 459 (src:7949-7952)
GIVEN `without lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowingly conveys it out of any of Her Majesty’s mints in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any machine, engine, tool, instrument, material or thing used or employed in connection with the manufacture of coins` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a useful part of anything mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `coin, bullion, metal or a mixture of metals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 459 the person commits the offence of conveying instruments for coining out of a mint` MEANS
    IF `without lawful justification or excuse` AND `knowingly conveys it out of any of Her Majesty’s mints in Canada`
        AND (`any machine, engine, tool, instrument, material or thing used or employed in connection with the manufacture of coins`   -- (a)
             OR `a useful part of anything mentioned in paragraph (a)`   -- (b)
             OR `coin, bullion, metal or a mixture of metals`)   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful justification or excuse, knowingly conveys out of any of Her Majesty’s mints in Canada"

@ref s 459 (src:7949)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 459 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 459 (src:7949)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 459 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `fourteen years`

§§ `s 460 -- Advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.`

-- src:7956 | 460 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:7957 | (a) by an advertisement or any other writing, offers to sell, procure or dispose of counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value or to give information with respect to the manner in which or the means by which counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value may be sold, procured or disposed of, or
-- src:7958 | (b) purchases, obtains, negotiates or otherwise deals with counterfeit tokens of value, or offers to negotiate with a view to purchasing or obtaining them.
@ref s 460(1) (src:7956-7958)
GIVEN `the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a counterfeit token of value, by s 448 counterfeit token of value` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by an advertisement or any other writing, offers to sell, procure or dispose of it or to give information with respect to the manner in which or the means by which it may be sold, procured or disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `purchases, obtains, negotiates or otherwise deals with it, or offers to negotiate with a view to purchasing or obtaining it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 460(1) the person commits the offence of advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.` MEANS
    IF (`by an advertisement or any other writing, offers to sell, procure or dispose of it or to give information with respect to the manner in which or the means by which it may be sold, procured or disposed of`
            AND (`the thing is counterfeit money, by s 448 counterfeit money` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 OR `the thing is a counterfeit token of value, by s 448 counterfeit token of value` EQUALS JUST TRUE))   -- (a)
        OR (`purchases, obtains, negotiates or otherwise deals with it, or offers to negotiate with a view to purchasing or obtaining it`
            AND `the thing is a counterfeit token of value, by s 448 counterfeit token of value` EQUALS JUST TRUE)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by an advertisement or any other writing, offers to sell, procure or dispose of counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value"

@ref s 460(1) (src:7956)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 460(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 460(1) (src:7956)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 460(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 449 punishment by indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `five years`
       , `s 454 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`

-- src:7960 | (2) No person shall be convicted of an offence under subsection (1) in respect of genuine coin or genuine paper money that has no value as money unless, at the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed, he knew that the coin or paper money had no value as money and he had a fraudulent intent in his dealings with or with respect to the coin or paper money.
@ref s 460(2) (src:7960)
GIVEN `the offence under subsection (1) is in respect of genuine coin or genuine paper money that has no value as money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed, they knew that the coin or paper money had no value as money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they had a fraudulent intent in their dealings with or with respect to the coin or paper money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 460(2) the bar on conviction applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence under subsection (1) is in respect of genuine coin or genuine paper money that has no value as money`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of genuine coin or genuine paper money that has no value as money"
    ELSE IF `at the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed, they knew that the coin or paper money had no value as money`
            AND `they had a fraudulent intent in their dealings with or with respect to the coin or paper money`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, at the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed, he knew that the coin or paper money had no value as money and he had a fraudulent intent" (the unless is met, so the bar does not apply)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 461 -- Special Provisions as to Proof`

-- src:7964 | 461 (1) Every offence relating to counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value shall be deemed to be complete notwithstanding that the money or tokens of value in respect of which the proceedings are taken are not finished or perfected or do not copy exactly the money or tokens of value that they are apparently intended to resemble or for which they are apparently intended to pass.
@ref s 461(1) (src:7964)
GIVEN `the offence relates to counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money or tokens of value in respect of which the proceedings are taken are not finished or perfected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money or tokens of value do not copy exactly the money or tokens of value that they are apparently intended to resemble or for which they are apparently intended to pass` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(1) the offence is deemed complete` MEANS
    IF `the offence relates to counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value`
        AND (`the money or tokens of value in respect of which the proceedings are taken are not finished or perfected`
             OR `the money or tokens of value do not copy exactly the money or tokens of value that they are apparently intended to resemble or for which they are apparently intended to pass`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every offence relating to counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value shall be deemed to be complete notwithstanding"

-- src:7966 | (2) In any proceedings under this Part, a certificate signed by a person designated as an examiner of counterfeit by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, stating that any coin, paper money or bank-note described therein is counterfeit money or that any coin, paper money or bank-note described therein is genuine and is or is not, as the case may be, current in Canada or elsewhere, is evidence of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref s 461(2) (src:7966)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is signed by a person designated as an examiner of counterfeit by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the coin, paper money or bank-note described in it is counterfeit money, or is genuine and is or is not current in Canada or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(2) the certificate is evidence of its statements without proof of the signature` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part`
        AND `the certificate is signed by a person designated as an examiner of counterfeit by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
        AND `the certificate states that the coin, paper money or bank-note described in it is counterfeit money, or is genuine and is or is not current in Canada or elsewhere`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings under this Part, a certificate signed by a person designated as an examiner of counterfeit"

-- src:7968 | (3) No certificate shall be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the other party reasonable notice of their intention and a copy of the certificate.
@ref s 461(3) (src:7968)
GIVEN `the party intending to produce the certificate has, before the trial, given to the other party reasonable notice of their intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has given the other party a copy of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(3) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the party intending to produce the certificate has, before the trial, given to the other party reasonable notice of their intention`
        AND `the party has given the other party a copy of the certificate`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No certificate shall be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the other party reasonable notice of their intention and a copy of the certificate" (the unless is met, so the bar does not apply)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:7970 | (4) A party against whom the certificate is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination.
@ref s 461(4) (src:7970)
GIVEN `the party is a party against whom the certificate is produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 461(4) the party may require the signer of the certificate to attend for cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the party is a party against whom the certificate is produced` AND `the court has given leave`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate"

§§ `s 462 -- Forfeiture`

-- src:7974 | 462 (1) Counterfeit money, counterfeit tokens of value and anything that is used or is intended to be used to make counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value belong to Her Majesty.
@ref s 462(1) (src:7974)
GIVEN `counterfeit money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `counterfeit tokens of value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `anything that is used or is intended to be used to make counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462(1) the thing belongs to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `counterfeit money` OR `counterfeit tokens of value` OR `anything that is used or is intended to be used to make counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Counterfeit money, counterfeit tokens of value and anything that is used or is intended to be used to make counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value belong to Her Majesty"

-- src:7976 | (2) A peace officer may seize and detain
-- src:7977 | (a) counterfeit money,
-- src:7978 | (b) counterfeit tokens of value, and
-- src:7979 | (c) machines, engines, tools, instruments, materials or things that have been used or that have been adapted and are intended for use in making counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value,
@ref s 462(2) (src:7976-7979)
GIVEN `counterfeit money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `counterfeit tokens of value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `machines, engines, tools, instruments, materials or things that have been used or that have been adapted and are intended for use in making counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462(2) a peace officer may seize and detain the thing` MEANS
    IF `counterfeit money` OR `counterfeit tokens of value`
        OR `machines, engines, tools, instruments, materials or things that have been used or that have been adapted and are intended for use in making counterfeit money or counterfeit tokens of value`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A peace officer may seize and detain"

-- src:7980 | and anything seized shall be sent to the Minister of Finance to be disposed of or dealt with as he may direct, but anything that is required as evidence in any proceedings shall not be sent to the Minister until it is no longer required in those proceedings.
@ref s 462(2) (src:7980)
GIVEN `the thing seized is required as evidence in any proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462(2) the thing seized is to be sent to the Minister of Finance now` MEANS
    IF `the thing seized is required as evidence in any proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "anything that is required as evidence in any proceedings shall not be sent to the Minister until it is no longer required in those proceedings"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

